    "title": "Republic",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Republic is a government type in which the ruler is elected from the citizenry, via the Open Elective succession law. Because there is no dynastic persistence between rulers, Republic governments are not playable . They are the  government type of cities."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In general, ruling over republics is similar to ruling merchant republics , except for a few key differences. While not as powerful, and unable to create trade posts, regular republics actually pay more in taxes to their liege lords and aren't quite as dangerous to their lieges."
                }
            ]
        },
